"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"mentioned","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-08-14T09:15:00Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":3655453366,"node_id":"MDE1OlN1YnNjcmliZWRFdmVudDM2NTU0NTMzNjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/events/3655453366","actor":{"login":"perminovs","id":22597273,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTk3Mjcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22597273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs","html_url":"https://github.com/perminovs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-08-14T09:15:00Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/673989041","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1835#issuecomment-673989041","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1835","id":673989041,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY3Mzk4OTA0MQ==","user":{"login":"perminovs","id":22597273,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTk3Mjcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22597273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs","html_url":"https://github.com/perminovs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-08-14T09:40:07Z","updated_at":"2020-08-14T09:44:30Z","body":"> Fixing this would be trivial but IMO it's very weird to write Field('a', ...) (so writing a default value) but still expect it to be required.\r\n\r\nYes, I'll show our use case for clarifying why we want to use Field with both default and const.\r\nWe have json messages with the same structure. While processing we want to hold it as different classes instance, which depends on 'type' value. So we have something like that:\r\n```py\r\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\r\n\r\nclass CreateSomeEntity(BaseModel):\r\n    type: str = Field('create', const=True)\r\n    id: int\r\n    value: str\r\n\r\nclass UpdateSomeEntity(BaseModel):\r\n    type: str = Field('update', const=True)\r\n    id: int\r\n    value: str\r\n\r\ndef deserialize(raw):\r\n    for klass in (CreateSomeEntity, UpdateSomeEntity):\r\n        try:\r\n            return klass.parse_obj(raw)\r\n        except ValueError:\r\n            pass\r\n    raise ValueError(f'cannot parse\\n{raw}')\r\n\r\ninvalid_input = {'id': 1, 'value': 'value'}\r\nmodel = deserialize(invalid_input)  # does not raise\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat's why successful parsing of `{'id': 1, 'value': 'value'}` is confusing. May be I should provided this example when I had opened the issue :smile: ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/673989041/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"perminovs","id":22597273,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNTk3Mjcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22597273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs","html_url":"https://github.com/perminovs","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/perminovs/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/674002810","html_url":"https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1835#issuecomment-674002810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/1835","id":674002810,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY3NDAwMjgxMA==","user":{"login":"PrettyWood","id":18406791,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDA2Nzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18406791?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PrettyWood","html_