ntagu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-05-17T13:32:18Z","updated_at":"2023-05-17T13:32:18Z","body":"Because we have removed the `const` argument to `Field` in V2, and `Literal` is handled properly, I'm going to consider this issue completed and will close it.\r\n\r\nRegarding how to annotate a field as a list of a few allowed literal values — you can actually put multiple items in a literal:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass Model(BaseModel):\r\n    literal_json_list: List[Literal[\"foo\", \"bar\"]]\r\n```\r\nYou won't be able to enforce the order of the items or length of them like this, but it will at least require that it be a list of just those two literal strings.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pydantic/pydantic/issues/comments/1551407247/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"dmontagu","id":35119617,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTE5NjE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35119617?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu","html_url":"https://github.com/dmontagu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dmontagu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.gi